# Full-scene warroom captures are working artefacts, not evidence.
# At deviceScaleFactor 3 a 1920x1080 scene is ~8-10 MB, and the -board / -map crops
# already carry every claim the scene shot would. Three of them were tracked briefly
# (PR #516) and account for 30 MB that every clone would have carried.
logs/**/shots/*-scene.png

# ── Generated run evidence under logs/ ────────────────────────────────────────
# These directories hold scenario-run and capture artefacts: 6.1 GB of them, with
# logs/r7-english-readability alone at 5.3 GB. They are cited BY PATH from ~20 tracked
# docs and must be preserved on disk — ignoring them changes nothing about the files.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS THAT THE TREE BE CLEAN: the gated 188-week entrypoint REFUSES to run on a
# dirty tree, and deliberately measures dirtiness whole-tree ("its one unique job is
# catching engine changes the consumed-input hashes structurally cannot see"). 320 untracked
# log files were therefore enough to block a baseline re-pin outright.
#
# Each of these already contains TRACKED files. gitignore does not untrack anything, so
# those stay versioned and keep showing up in diffs; only the untracked spill goes quiet.
# CONSEQUENCE TO KNOW: a genuinely new piece of evidence in one of these needs `git add -f`.
# That is the trade — and it matches the repo's own rule that generated logs live in
# excluded roots while executable harnesses live in tracked tools/.
logs/bounded-deletion-cleanup/
logs/r7-english-readability/
logs/r8-decision-command-usability/
logs/r9-build-preparation/
logs/branch-hygiene/
logs/local-llm/
